### FINDING_1:
- **Reviewer(s)**: Cursor-dyn-marker-contract
- **Severity**: important
- **Focus area**: correctness
- **Location**: skills/review/scripts/aggregate-findings.sh:637-696
- **Concern**: Plan-mode tagged split does not reconcile with the existing validate-then-move merge pipeline. Scenario: aggregate-findings.sh validates the raw LLM candidate against the full FINDINGS_FILE (input reviewers must all appear in candidate) before mv to findings-in-scope.md; excluding tagged blocks from the LLM prompt but leaving validate_py unchanged will fail whenever a tagged block is the sole finding for a reviewer slot, forcing AGGREGATED=false fallback and dropping the intended conservative-merge path
- **Proposed resolution**: In plan mode, build the LLM prompt from untagged blocks only, append tagged blocks after a successful untagged merge, and run marker/reviewer validation on the combined output (or validate untagged-only input against the LLM candidate plus a separate tagged-preservation gate)

### FINDING_2:
- **Reviewer(s)**: Cursor-dyn-marker-contract
- **Severity**: important
- **Focus area**: correctness
- **Location**: skills/design/scripts/plan-review-loop.sh:1106-1285
- **Concern**: Post-dedup parity fallback has no staged pre-dedup in-scope artifact. Scenario: The loop only materializes _findings_tmp then deduped findings.md then split findings-in-scope.md; parity failure cannot fall back to a pre-dedup in-scope stream without first persisting a pre-dedup split (or re-splitting _findings_tmp) and wiring that path to skip or replace post-dedup findings-in-scope.md before aggregation
- **Proposed resolution**: Before the Jaccard deduper runs, split _findings_tmp into findings-in-scope.pre-dedup.md (and OOS if needed), run dedup/parity against that snapshot, and on parity failure copy the pre-dedup in-scope file to findings-in-scope.md before aggregation

### FINDING_3:
- **Reviewer(s)**: Cursor-dyn-marker-contract
- **Severity**: important
- **Focus area**: correctness
- **Location**: skills/design/scripts/plan-review-loop.sh:997-1012
- **Concern**: Production /design marker shape is the inline TSV emitter not collect-findings.sh. Scenario: /design converts reviewer TSV via embedded Python into separate **Severity** plus **Concern** lines (Concern carries raw what text), while collect-findings.sh folds severity into the Concern body as [important] what; detector tests that only exercise collect-findings.sh miss the live Concern format and can pass while production markers fail after dedup/aggregation
- **Proposed resolution**: Add test-plan-review-loop or test-check-scope-reduction-marker fixtures that use the inline emitter shape (- **Severity**: important / - **Concern**: [SCOPE-REDUCTION] ...) and assert detection after collect, dedup, and plan-mode aggregation

### FINDING_4:
- **Reviewer(s)**: Cursor-dyn-marker-contract
- **Severity**: important
- **Focus area**: risk-integration
- **Location**: skills/design/scripts/plan-review-loop.sh:1172-1185
- **Concern**: Dedup merge order can drop a leading marker before parity runs. Scenario: Current dedup keeps the first Jaccard match and merge_reviewers(kb, blk) discards the later body; an untagged block that appears before a tagged duplicate will lose [SCOPE-REDUCTION] until parity fallback fires, adding an extra degraded ballot path and relying on parity heuristics rather than deterministic tagged-wins merge
- **Proposed resolution**: Implement the planned tagged-wins rule inside the dedup loop (prefer tagged body or reinsert leading marker before parity) so tagged markers survive the primary path without depending on fallback

### FINDING_1:
- **Reviewer(s)**: Codex-dyn-marker-contract
- **Severity**: important
- **Focus area**: correctness
- **Location**: skills/design/scripts/plan-review-loop.sh:1000-1085,1199-1202,1285-1359; scripts/lib-vote-tally.sh:103-118
- **Concern**: Proposed marker-preservation fallback can bypass the only FINDING/OOS renumbering pass. Scenario: Raw per-reviewer fragments restart at FINDING_1/OOS_1, and the plan says to append tagged blocks verbatim or fall back to pre-dedup streams; a tagged original FINDING_1 plus an aggregated untagged FINDING_1 makes split_ballot_to_blocks abort as a duplicate heading before voting/tally
- **Proposed resolution**: Keep the minimum contract by adding one final sequential renumber step after any tagged append or pre-dedup fallback and before ballot.txt; preserve block bodies and leading markers, only rewrite headings

### FINDING_2:
- **Reviewer(s)**: Codex-dyn-marker-contract
- **Severity**: latent
- **Focus area**: correctness
- **Location**: skills/design/scripts/plan-review-loop.sh:1114-1180; skills/review/scripts/aggregate-findings.sh:168-172
- **Concern**: Jaccard duplicate detection still compares the marker words as problem words. Scenario: A short tagged finding [SCOPE-REDUCTION] Remove Redis and an untagged duplicate Remove Redis share only 2 of 4 tokens, so the >0.6 merge can miss it; aggregation then excludes the tagged block and cannot repair the duplicate, leaving two ballot findings for one scope cut
- **Proposed resolution**: Strip one leading severity bracket and [SCOPE-REDUCTION] from the comparison text used by dedup/parity only, then keep the tagged body when a merge occurs.

